.TH UNITDECK 1 "2026" "UnitDeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unitdeck \- manage systemd system and user services from a graphical interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unitdeck
.RI [ \-\-version ]
.RI [ \-\-check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
UnitDeck lists the .service units of the system manager and of the user session,
starts, stops, restarts, enables, masks and edits them (with drop-ins), creates new
services from templates and shows their journal, with live updates over D-Bus.
.PP
It always runs as a normal user and refuses to start as root. Privileged actions are
authorized through polkit; system unit files are written by the helper
.I /usr/libexec/unitdeck/unitdeck-helper
launched with pkexec.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Load Qt and exit; used to verify an installation without opening a window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system, ~/.config/systemd/user
Where system and user units created or overridden by UnitDeck are written.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/eu.nicop.unitdeck.policy
Polkit policy of the helper (auth_admin_keep by default).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Palmieri (n1c0p), https://github.com/n1c0p/UnitDeck
